        <StdOut>Set apart for WebKit: F-5: WebKit hints the glyphs of the faces the document embeds, as its Linux build does whatever fontconfig, text-rendering or its own settings say, while Chromium draws them unhinted. WebKit's image of hiddensymbols has 7 pixels outside the tolerance of Chromium's (each color channel within the range the other image takes within 1 pixel, give or take 4 levels, or at an edge within 80 levels of it, and within 0.4 of the contrast around it, once both are blurred by 1 pixel), by up to 3 levels; see browsers/webkit/differences/hiddensymbols.png.</StdOut>
